escription":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":245,"end":245,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":247,"end":247,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":253,"end":253,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":257,"end":257,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":295,"end":295,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":299,"end":299,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"DNA binding","start":305,"end":400,"description":"Fork-head"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":416,"end":416,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":420,"end":420,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":422,"end":422,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":428,"end":428,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":436,"end":436,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":441,"end":441,"description":"Phosphoserine; by PKC/PRKCB"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":445,"end":445,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":459,"end":459,"description":"Phosphoserine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Interacts with SIN3A and SIN3B (via PAH2) to form a complex which represses transcription (By similarity). Component of SIN3A-, but not SIN3B-, containing multiprotein complexes (By similarity). Interacts with FOXO4 and MEF2C; both interactions inhibit FOXO4 and MEF2C transactivation activity (By similarity). Interacts (when phosphorylated) with YWHAE/14-3-3-epsilon; promotes sequestration in the cytoplasm and leads to impaired ability to bind DNA (By similarity). Interacts with FHL2 (By similarity). Interacts with SRF (PubMed:17670796). Interacts with DVL2 and DVL3; the interaction induces DVL2 nuclear translocation (PubMed:25805136). Interacts with BAP1 (when phosphorylated) (PubMed:25451922). Accessory component of the polycomb repressive deubiquitinase (PR-DUB) complex, at least composed of BAP1, one of ASXL1, ASXL2 or (probably) ASXL3 and one of MBD5 or MBD6 (PubMed:24634419, PubMed:30664650). The PR-DUB core associates with a number of accessory proteins, including FOXK1, FOXK2, KDM1B, HCFC1 and OGT (Probable) (PubMed:30664650)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"P85037-2","name":"2","synonyms":["b"],"notes":[],"length":570,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,2],[25,188,546]],"edits":[{"start":1,"end":187,"original":"MAEVGEDSGARALLALRSAPCSPVLCAAAAAAAFPAAAPP","replacement":"MAYCLGVNFVPSRFCYQLHRLLLR","added":24}],"missing":185,"replaced":0,"novel":22,"foldedAbsent":97,"foldedMissing":97,"features":[[1,38,0],[2,93,0],[3,1,0],[4,53,0],[5,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-P85037-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P85037-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":52.9,"plddt":[[0,21],[50,3],[70,16],[50,4],[0,11],[50,1],[0,2],[50,1],[0,1],[50,2],[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,4],[0,1],[50,1],[0,6],[50,4],[0,5],[50,1],[0,4],[50,1],[0,16],[50,2],[70,14],[50,7],[0,3],[50,5],[70,3],[90,38],[70,2],[90,23],[70,7],[90,19],[70,3],[50,3],[0,2],[50,1],[0,3],[50,2],[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,4],[50,3],[0,1],[50,1],[0,5],[50,1],[0,6],[50,1],[0,52],[50,1],[0,6],[50,1],[0,152],[50,1],[0,22],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,53],[50,8]],"losingConfidence":0}}],"ensemblGenes":["ENSG00000164916.12"],"unmapped":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[]},"coding":{"genes":1,"gencode":2,"mapped":1},"explorer":{"gene":null,"isoforms":null},"locus":"chr7:4682295-4771442","exons":{"transcript":"ENST00000328914.5","first":1,"junctions":[560,746,903,1050,1244,1411,1696,1921]},"structures":{"P85037-1":{"transcript":"ENST00000328914.5","strand":1,"coding":[4682309,4762464],"exons":[[4682295,4682868],[4740838,4741023],[4754459,4754615],[4755237,4755383],[4756994,4757187],[4759051,4759217],[4759311,4